      <data key="d0">BLOOD TEST</data>
      <data key="d1">BLOOD TEST</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">A blood test is a laboratory procedure in which a needle is inserted into a vein to collect a blood sample. The sample is then examined in a lab to detect signs of disease, monitor health conditions, or evaluate organ function. Blood tests may be ordered if a recurrence of a condition is suspected, and common tests include a complete blood count (CBC), blood urea nitrogen (BUN), creatinine, and liver function tests, which assess kidney and liver health. It is recommended that blood test results be kept in a medical binder for organized record-keeping and future reference.
**Relationships:** (No explicit relationships listed in the data tables)</data>
