    <node id="HISTOLOGY">
      <data key="d0">HISTOLOGY</data>
      <data key="d1">HISTOLOGY</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Histology is the study of the anatomy of cells, tissues, and organs under a microscope, and it is also a key process used to guide clinical decision-making. In practice, histology involves the evaluation of the structure of cells or tissues at the microscopic level, typically performed by a neuropathologist on biopsy tissue. This examination is essential for classifying tumors, as the microscopic features of the tissue help determine the precise diagnosis. By revealing the cellular architecture and identifying abnormalities, histology provides critical information that is used to make treatment decisions. Whether described as a broad scientific discipline or a specific diagnostic procedure, histology serves as a foundational tool in both understanding normal biological structure and diagnosing disease, particularly in the context of neuropathology and oncology.
Relationships:
  - Source: TREATMENT
  - Target: HISTOLOGY
  - Description: Histology is used to make treatment decisions.
  - Source: HISTOLOGY
  - Target: BIOPSY
  - Description: Histologic analysis is performed on tissue obtained from a biopsy.
  - Source: BIOPSY
  - Target: HISTOLOGY
  - Description: Biopsy tissue samples are studied by histology.
  - Source: HISTOLOGY
  - Target: TREATMENT TEAM
  - Description: Histology helps classify the tumor and contributes to the full description used to plan treatment.
  - Source: HISTOLOGY
  - Target: PATHOLOGIST
  - Description: A pathologist examines tissue samples and provides histology information in a pathology report.
  - Source: HISTOLOGY
  - Target: NEUROSURGEON
  - Description: Histology results help the neurosurgeon decide how much of the tumor to remove.
  - Source: HISTOLOGY
  - Target: NEUROPATHOLOGIST
  - Description: The neuropathologist performs histologic analysis when inspecting tissue under a microscope.
  - Source: OPEN BIOPSY
  - Target: HISTOLOGY
  - Description: Open biopsy may be recommended to confirm histology.
  - Source: LAB TESTING
  - Target: HISTOLOGY
  - Description: Histology is part of lab testing and is performed on biopsy tissue.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
