    <node id="OPEN BIOPSY">
      <data key="d0">OPEN BIOPSY</data>
      <data key="d1">OPEN BIOPSY</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">Open biopsy is a surgical biopsy procedure in which a neurosurgeon performs a craniotomy, opening the scalp and skull to remove pieces of tumor tissue. It is one of the two standard types of biopsies used for gliomas, and it serves as a surgical procedure to excise a tumor in order to confirm its histology.
**Relationships:**
  - Source: OPEN BIOPSY
  - Target: NEUROSURGEON
  - Description: The neurosurgeon performs an open biopsy by opening the scalp and skull to remove tumor pieces.
  - Source: OPEN BIOPSY
  - Target: NEUROPATHOLOGIST
  - Description: Tissue from an open biopsy is examined by the neuropathologist.</data>
    </node>
