Overall, the American Joint Committee on Cancer serves as the authoritative organization for cancer staging, providing a standardized method for clinicians to describe cancer extent, location, and subtype, and to communicate prognosis across different malignancies. Its staging framework is integral to cancer diagnosis, treatment planning, and research, ensuring consistent classification for a broad range of cancers.
