      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Surgery is a type of treatment, specifically a form of cancer treatment. It is one of the main treatment options available for cancer, including cervical cancer, where it is recognized as a primary treatment approach. Surgery can also be combined with other therapies; when drug therapy is administered before surgery, the pathologic stage of the disease may include a "y" prefix to indicate this sequence. As a treatment modality, surgery plays a key role in the management of cancer and is included among the main types of treatment for cervical cancer.
  - Source: TREATMENT
  - Target: SURGERY
  - Description: Surgery is a type of cancer treatment
  - Source: SURGERY
  - Target: RADIATION THERAPY
  - Description: Surgery and radiation therapy are two established cancer treatment modalities that can be used alone, together, or in sequence. Both are recognized treatment options for cancers such as thyroid cancer and squamous cell skin cancer. Their specific relationship depends on the clinical situation.</data>
