    <node id="TUMOR MUTATION TESTING">
      <data key="d0">TUMOR MUTATION TESTING</data>
      <data key="d1">TUMOR MUTATION TESTING</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">TUMOR MUTATION TESTING is a diagnostic approach that analyzes a sample of tumor tissue or blood to detect DNA mutations present in cancer cells. This testing enables the identification of specific genetic alterations that may guide targeted therapy, allowing treatment to be tailored to the molecular characteristics of a patient's tumor. A key function of tumor mutation testing is its ability to distinguish somatic mutations—those acquired in cancer cells—from inherited (germline) mutations, which is important for determining whether a mutation is tumor-specific or hereditary. This testing is closely related to biomarker testing and molecular profiling, as it looks for mutations in tumor DNA to inform diagnosis, prognosis, and treatment decisions. In summary, tumor mutation testing is a precision medicine tool that uses genetic information from tumors to support personalized cancer care.
Relationships: None listed</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
