    <node id="PROLONGED CORRECTED QT INTERVAL (QTC): THIS CONDITION OCCURS WHEN THE HEART MUSCLE TAKES LONGER THAN NORMAL TO RECHARGE BETWEEN BEATS. CERTAIN CANCER TREATMENTS CAN CAUSE THIS, AND A TOO-PROLONGED QTC CAN LEAD TO DANGEROUS HEART RHYTHMS [DATA: ENTITIES (450, 470); RELATIONSHIPS (930, 934, 933)]. AN ELECTROCARDIOGRAM (ECG OR EKG) IS THE PRIMARY TEST USED TO DETECT THIS CONDITION, AS IT SHOWS ELECTRICAL CHANGES IN THE HEART, INCLUDING HEART RATE AND RHYTHM [DATA: ENTITIES (448, 514); RELATIONSHIPS (930, 1025)].">
