    <node id="PROLONGED CORRECTED QT INTERVAL (QTC)">
      <data key="d0">PROLONGED CORRECTED QT INTERVAL (QTC)</data>
      <data key="d1">PROLONGED CORRECTED QT INTERVAL (QTC)</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3" />
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">: This condition occurs when the heart muscle takes longer than normal to recharge between beats. Certain cancer treatments can cause this, and a too-prolonged QTc can lead to dangerous heart rhythms [Data: Entities (450, 470); Relationships (930, 934, 933)]. An electrocardiogram (ECG or EKG) is the primary test used to detect this condition, as it shows electrical changes in the heart, including heart rate and rhythm [Data: Entities (448, 514); Relationships (930, 1025)].
</data>
    </node>
