    <node id="STEM CELL RESCUE">
      <data key="d0">STEM CELL RESCUE</data>
      <data key="d1">STEM CELL RESCUE</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">(No description provided in the data tables)
Relationships:
  - Source: STEM CELL RESCUE
  - Target: HIGH-DOSE CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Description: Stem cell rescue is a medical procedure used in the treatment of lymphoma, and high-dose chemotherapy is a critical component of this process. High-dose chemotherapy is administered as a key step in stem cell rescue, specifically designed to kill lymphoma cells before the replacement of stem cells takes place. It serves as the second, cell-destroying step of the overall stem cell rescue procedure, highlighting its role in eradicating malignant cells to prepare the body for new, healthy stem cells. Together, these entities form a treatment strategy in which high-dose chemotherapy clears the way for stem cell replacement, making it an essential part of the rescue process.</data>
    </node>
