    <node id="PSA DENSITY">
      <data key="d0">PSA DENSITY</data>
      <data key="d1">PSA DENSITY</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">(Referenced in relationships; PSA density calculated using prostate size from MRI)
Relationships:
  - Source: PSA DENSITY
  - Target: MRI SCAN
  - Description: PSA density is a clinical metric calculated using prostate size, which is measured via an MRI scan. The MRI scan provides an accurate measurement of prostate volume, and this measurement is then used in conjunction with the serum PSA (prostate-specific antigen) level to derive the PSA density. Thus, the MRI scan plays a key role in determining PSA density, which helps in assessing prostate-related conditions.

---</data>
