      <data key="d3">Squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) is closely associated with head and neck cancer. As the most common type of mouth cancer, and since mouth cancer is a type of head and neck cancer, SCC is a significant subtype within this broader category. Additionally, squamous cell carcinoma arising in the nasopharynx is also a form of head and neck cancer. Therefore, SCC can manifest in various locations within the head and neck region, including the oral cavity and nasopharynx, and is recognized as a major histological type of head and neck cancer.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">ENTITY: RELATIONSHIP: HEAD AND NECK CANCER to SQUAMOUS CELL CARCINOMA
Description: Squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) is closely associated with head and neck cancer. As the most common type of mouth cancer, and since mouth cancer is a type of head and neck cancer, SCC is a significant subtype within this broader category. Additionally, squamous cell carcinoma arising in the nasopharynx is also a form of head and neck cancer. Therefore, SCC can manifest in various locations within the head and neck region, including the oral cavity and nasopharynx, and is recognized as a major histological type of head and neck cancer.</data>
    </node>
