      <data key="d3">Squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) is the most common type of mouth cancer. Mouth cancer encompasses various malignancies, and among them, squamous cell carcinoma is the most frequently diagnosed form. Both statements confirm that SCC, also referred to as squamous cell carcinoma, represents the predominant subtype of mouth cancer.</data>
