    <node id="EXTRAFASCIAL HYSTERECTOMY">
      <data key="d0">EXTRAFASCIAL HYSTERECTOMY</data>
      <data key="d1">EXTRAFASCIAL HYSTERECTOMY</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
      <data key="d3">Extrafascial hysterectomy is a simple hysterectomy that removes only the uterus, including the cervix. It can be performed vaginally, abdominally, or using minimally invasive techniques. This procedure is used for the non-fertility-sparing treatment of certain early-stage cervical cancers, specifically including stage IA1 cancer.
Relationships:
  - Source: EXTRAFASCIAL HYSTERECTOMY
  - Target: MODIFIED RADICAL HYSTERECTOMY
  - Description: Extrafascial hysterectomy and modified radical hysterectomy are alternative options when pre-cancer is found at cone biopsy margins
  - Source: CERVICAL CANCER
  - Target: EXTRAFASCIAL HYSTERECTOMY
  - Description: Extrafascial hysterectomy is most commonly used for stage IA1 cervical cancer
  - Source: EXTRAFASCIAL HYSTERECTOMY
  - Target: PELVIC LYMPH NODE EVALUATION
  - Description: Pelvic lymph node evaluation is performed with extrafascial hysterectomy
  - Source: EXTRAFASCIAL HYSTERECTOMY
  - Target: SURVEILLANCE
  - Description: Surveillance begins after extrafascial hysterectomy
  - Source: EXTRAFASCIAL HYSTERECTOMY
  - Target: STAGE IA1 CANCER
  - Description: Extrafascial hysterectomy is most commonly used for stage IA1 cancer</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIGITAL RECTAL EXAMINATION">
      <data key="d0">DIGITAL RECTAL EXAMINATION</data>
      <data key="d1">DIGITAL RECTAL EXAMINATION</data>
      <data key="d2">endpoint</data>
