    <node id="THIS GENETIC ABNORMALITY IS A DEFINING FEATURE OF THE DISEASE AND DRIVES ITS CLINICAL BEHAVIOR. APL IS DISCUSSED IN CHAPTER 5 OF THE NCCN GUIDELINES FOR PATIENTS, WHICH PROVIDES INFORMATION ABOUT THIS SPECIFIC LEUKEMIA SUBTYPE. AS A DISTINCT FORM OF AML, APL REQUIRES SPECIALIZED DIAGNOSTIC EVALUATION AND MANAGEMENT APPROACHES DUE TO ITS UNIQUE GENETIC BASIS AND CLINICAL CHARACTERISTICS.">
      <data key="d0">THIS GENETIC ABNORMALITY IS A DEFINING FEATURE OF THE DISEASE AND DRIVES ITS CLINICAL BEHAVIOR. APL IS DISCUSSED IN CHAPTER 5 OF THE NCCN GUIDELINES FOR PATIENTS, WHICH PROVIDES INFORMATION ABOUT THIS SPECIFIC LEUKEMIA SUBTYPE. AS A DISTINCT FORM OF AML, APL REQUIRES SPECIALIZED DIAGNOSTIC EVALUATION AND MANAGEMENT APPROACHES DUE TO ITS UNIQUE GENETIC BASIS AND CLINICAL CHARACTERISTICS.</data>
      <data key="d1">THIS GENETIC ABNORMALITY IS A DEFINING FEATURE OF THE DISEASE AND DRIVES ITS CLINICAL BEHAVIOR. APL IS DISCUSSED IN CHAPTER 5 OF THE NCCN GUIDELINES FOR PATIENTS, WHICH PROVIDES INFORMATION ABOUT THIS SPECIFIC LEUKEMIA SUBTYPE. AS A DISTINCT FORM OF AML, APL REQUIRES SPECIALIZED DIAGNOSTIC EVALUATION AND MANAGEMENT APPROACHES DUE TO ITS UNIQUE GENETIC BASIS AND CLINICAL CHARACTERISTICS.</data>
