    <node id="BLUE LIGHT CYSTOSCOPY">
      <data key="d0">BLUE LIGHT CYSTOSCOPY</data>
      <data key="d1">BLUE LIGHT CYSTOSCOPY</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">A newer type of cystoscopy that uses blue light with a special dye injected into the bladder; may identify tumors more distinctly than white light; still in the testing phase
Relationships:
  - Source: CYSTOSCOPY
  - Target: BLUE LIGHT CYSTOSCOPY
  - Description: Cystoscopy is a medical procedure that allows doctors to examine the inside of the bladder and urethra. Blue light cystoscopy is a newer, specialized type of cystoscopy that enhances this examination. It uses blue light and a photosensitizing dye, which causes abnormal tissue to appear differently under the blue light, aiding in the detection and evaluation of conditions such as bladder cancer. Together, cystoscopy and blue light cystoscopy represent standard and advanced approaches to urological diagnosis and treatment.
  - Source: BLUE LIGHT CYSTOSCOPY
  - Target: NARROW-BAND IMAGING
  - Description: Both are newer detection techniques compared with white light cystoscopy and are still in the testing phase
  - Source: NARROW-BAND IMAGING
  - Target: BLUE LIGHT CYSTOSCOPY
  - Description: Both are relatively new imaging methods being tested for bladder tumor detection.
  - Source: WHITE LIGHT CYSTOSCOPY
  - Target: BLUE LIGHT CYSTOSCOPY
  - Description: Blue light cystoscopy may identify tumors more distinctly than standard white light cystoscopy
  - Source: WHITE LIGHT
  - Target: BLUE LIGHT CYSTOSCOPY
  - Description: Blue light cystoscopy is a newer method that may detect tumors better than standard white light detection.</data>
