      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">A lab test that analyzes urine for cancer or precancerous cells; done when blood is in urine; a sample may be collected during cystoscopy and examined by a pathologist
Relationships:
  - Source: URINE CYTOLOGY
  - Target: CYSTOSCOPY
  - Description: A urine sample can be collected during cystoscopy; if urine cytology finds abnormal cells, a cystoscopy is needed to locate cancer in the urethra or bladder
  - Source: URINE CYTOLOGY
  - Target: BIOPSY
  - Description: Abnormal urine cytology may lead to cystoscopy and biopsy to locate and test suspicious areas in the urinary tract
  - Source: URINE CYTOLOGY
  - Target: URINE TESTS FOR TUMOR MARKERS
  - Description: Both are urine-based tests used to look for signs of cancer in the urine</data>
