      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Partial cystectomy is a surgical procedure to remove part of the bladder. It is rarely used for the treatment of bladder cancer, as only a small proportion of patients are candidates for this approach: fewer than 1 in 20 people with bladder cancer are eligible for the procedure.
