    <node id="NUTRITION ASSESSMENT">
      <data key="d0">NUTRITION ASSESSMENT</data>
      <data key="d1">NUTRITION ASSESSMENT</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">NUTRITION ASSESSMENT is a structured consultation with a qualified nutrition expert—such as a nutritionist or dietitian—that takes place before the initiation of medical treatment, particularly in the context of cancer care. The primary purpose of this assessment is to ensure that the patient receives adequate nutrition to support their overall health and treatment outcomes. During the consultation, the nutrition expert evaluates the patient’s nutritional status and recommends appropriate foods and fluids tailored to the individual’s needs, thereby planning adequate food and fluid intake for the upcoming treatment period. This proactive planning helps address potential nutritional challenges that may arise during therapy. In addition to the initial consultation, the nutrition assessment includes ongoing monitoring by the treatment team during and after treatment. This follow-up ensures that the patient’s nutritional needs continue to be met, allowing for adjustments to the dietary plan as circumstances change. By integrating pre-treatment planning with continued supervision, the nutrition assessment serves as a vital component of comprehensive patient care, helping to optimize strength, recovery, and quality of life throughout the treatment journey.
Relationships: (No direct relationships listed in the provided data)</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
