    <node id="ADJUVANT THERAPY">
      <data key="d0">ADJUVANT THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d1">ADJUVANT THERAPY</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Adjuvant therapy is a systemic drug treatment administered after surgery, also referred to as postoperative therapy. It is given following primary treatment—such as surgical removal of a tumor—with the goal of lowering the risk that the cancer will return. In addition to systemic drugs, radiation therapy may also be used as adjuvant therapy after surgery.
Relationships: (No relationship records provided in data)</data>
