    <node id="EBRT">
      <data key="d0">EBRT</data>
      <data key="d1">EBRT</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">EBRT, or external beam radiation therapy, is a local treatment for cancerous lesions that delivers radiation from outside the body to a targeted area, such as the pelvis or a larger field. It is commonly recommended after surgery for local or regional recurrence, often in combination with systemic therapy. Additionally, EBRT may be administered with platinum chemotherapy as part of chemoradiation, enhancing its therapeutic effect. This summary incorporates all provided descriptions, highlighting EBRT's role as a localized treatment, its use in postoperative care for recurrent disease, and its integration with systemic and chemotherapeutic approaches.
Relationships: (No relationship records provided in data)</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">ENTITY: EBRT
Description: EBRT, or external beam radiation therapy, is a local treatment for cancerous lesions that delivers radiation from outside the body to a targeted area, such as the pelvis or a larger field. It is commonly recommended after surgery for local or regional recurrence, often in combination with systemic therapy. Additionally, EBRT may be administered with platinum chemotherapy as part of chemoradiation, enhancing its therapeutic effect. This summary incorporates all provided descriptions, highlighting EBRT's role as a localized treatment, its use in postoperative care for recurrent disease, and its integration with systemic and chemotherapeutic approaches.
Relationships: (No relationship records provided in data)</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY">
      <data key="d0">PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d1">PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Platinum chemotherapy is a type of cancer treatment that uses drugs containing the metal platinum. This category includes well-known agents such as cisplatin and carboplatin. It is commonly administered during radiation therapy, often concurrently with external beam radiation therapy (EBRT) as part of a chemoradiation regimen. This approach is specifically utilized in the treatment of cancers such as squamous cell skin cancer and cervical cancer, among others. As a systemic therapy, platinum chemotherapy works by interfering with DNA replication in rapidly dividing cancer cells, enhancing the effects of radiation when given together.
Relationships: (No relationship records provided in data)</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">ENTITY: PLATINUM CHEMOTHERAPY
Description: Platinum chemotherapy is a type of cancer treatment that uses drugs containing the metal platinum. This category includes well-known agents such as cisplatin and carboplatin. It is commonly administered during radiation therapy, often concurrently with external beam radiation therapy (EBRT) as part of a chemoradiation regimen. This approach is specifically utilized in the treatment of cancers such as squamous cell skin cancer and cervical cancer, among others. As a systemic therapy, platinum chemotherapy works by interfering with DNA replication in rapidly dividing cancer cells, enhancing the effects of radiation when given together.
Relationships: (No relationship records provided in data)</data>
    </node>
