    <node id="ENDOSCOPY">
      <data key="d0">ENDOSCOPY</data>
      <data key="d1">ENDOSCOPY</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Endoscopy is a medical scoping procedure in which an endoscope is guided into the body, typically through the mouth or nose, to look inside the body. It may be used to determine the size and spread of a tumor and to take a tumor sample. To ease the patient's discomfort, a topical spray numbs the throat. In the context of treatment planning, endoscopy is often combined with examination under anesthesia.
Relationships:
  - Source: SCOPING PROCEDURES
  - Target: ENDOSCOPY
  - Description: Endoscopy is a scoping procedure that uses an endoscope.</data>
