      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Radical trachelectomy is a fertility-sparing surgical procedure that removes the cervix and part of the upper vagina while preserving the uterus. As a specific type of trachelectomy, it also entails removal of the cervix along with approximately two centimeters of vaginal tissue. This approach is designed to treat certain gynecologic conditions while maintaining the potential for future childbearing.
