    <node id="BCG SHORTAGE">
      <data key="d0">BCG SHORTAGE</data>
      <data key="d1">BCG SHORTAGE</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">BCG shortage is the prolonged lack of sufficient BCG supply in the United States and worldwide, leading to reduced doses or alternative treatments for bladder cancer patients.
Relationships:
  - Source: CLINICAL TRIAL
  - Target: BCG SHORTAGE
  - Description: Joining a clinical trial is an option when regular BCG treatment is unavailable due to shortage.
  - Source: UNITED STATES
  - Target: BCG SHORTAGE
  - Description: The BCG shortage has been occurring in the United States for several years.
  - Source: INTRAVESICAL BCG THERAPY
  - Target: BCG SHORTAGE
  - Description: Because of the BCG shortage, many patients cannot receive intravesical BCG therapy or receive a reduced dose.
  - Source: INTRAVESICAL CHEMOTHERAPY
  - Target: BCG SHORTAGE
  - Description: If a regular course of BCG treatment isn't available due to shortage, intravesical chemotherapy may be offered instead.
  - Source: BCG THERAPY
  - Target: BCG SHORTAGE
  - Description: The BCG shortage affects the supply and use of BCG therapy.
  - Source: BLADDER REMOVAL SURGERY
  - Target: BCG SHORTAGE
  - Description: Bladder removal surgery is an option for high-risk patients if regular BCG treatment is unavailable due to shortage.
  - Source: BCG MAINTENANCE THERAPY
  - Target: BCG SHORTAGE
  - Description: During the BCG shortage, eliminating BCG maintenance therapy is one of the options considered.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
