    <node id="COLOANAL ANASTOMOSIS">
      <data key="d0">COLOANAL ANASTOMOSIS</data>
      <data key="d1">COLOANAL ANASTOMOSIS</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Coloanal anastomosis is the attachment of the colon directly to the anus during low anterior resection when colorectal reconnection is not possible.
Relationships:
  - Source: COLOANAL ANASTOMOSIS
  - Target: COLOSTOMY
  - Description: A colostomy may be made when the colon cannot be attached to the anus after low anterior resection
