      <data key="d3">Cervical biopsy is a diagnostic procedure in which small tissue samples are removed from the cervix and tested for dysplasia and cancer. It is the most commonly used procedure to diagnose cervical cancer, with the removed samples examined by a pathologist to determine the presence of abnormal or cancerous cells.
**Relationships:** None listed in the provided data</data>
