    <node id="RELATIONSHIP: COLONOSCOPY → POLYPECTOMY">
      <data key="d0">RELATIONSHIP: COLONOSCOPY → POLYPECTOMY</data>
      <data key="d1">RELATIONSHIP: COLONOSCOPY → POLYPECTOMY</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">Colonoscopy and polypectomy are directly connected medical procedures, as polypectomy is performed during a colonoscopy. A colonoscopy is a diagnostic and therapeutic procedure that allows a physician to visually examine the interior of the colon. When polyps are detected during this examination, they are typically removed right away using a polypectomy. Polypectomy is a minor surgical procedure specifically designed to remove polyps from the lining of the colon. Most polyps can be successfully removed in this manner during a colonoscopy, making polypectomy the standard method for polyp removal. Thus, the two procedures are integrally linked, with colonoscopy providing the access and visualization needed for the polypectomy to be performed safely and effectively.</data>
      <data key="d4">1</data>
      <data key="d5">0</data>
      <data key="d6">ENTITY: RELATIONSHIP: COLONOSCOPY → POLYPECTOMY
Description: Colonoscopy and polypectomy are directly connected medical procedures, as polypectomy is performed during a colonoscopy. A colonoscopy is a diagnostic and therapeutic procedure that allows a physician to visually examine the interior of the colon. When polyps are detected during this examination, they are typically removed right away using a polypectomy. Polypectomy is a minor surgical procedure specifically designed to remove polyps from the lining of the colon. Most polyps can be successfully removed in this manner during a colonoscopy, making polypectomy the standard method for polyp removal. Thus, the two procedures are integrally linked, with colonoscopy providing the access and visualization needed for the polypectomy to be performed safely and effectively.</data>
    </node>
