    <node id="SODIUM FLUORIDE PET/CT">
      <data key="d0">SODIUM FLUORIDE PET/CT</data>
      <data key="d1">SODIUM FLUORIDE PET/CT</data>
      <data key="d2">extracted</data>
      <data key="d3">SODIUM FLUORIDE PET/CT is a bone imaging test used to evaluate skeletal conditions. It may not be necessary in cases where an FDG-PET/CT scan has already clearly demonstrated the presence of cancer in the bone. In such instances, the additional sodium fluoride PET/CT provides redundant information and can be avoided.
Relationships:
  - Source: FDG-PET/CT
  - Target: SODIUM FLUORIDE PET/CT
  - Description: FDG-PET/CT and sodium fluoride PET/CT are two imaging techniques used to evaluate cancer, particularly in bone. When FDG-PET/CT clearly demonstrates the presence of cancer in the bone, a subsequent sodium fluoride PET/CT scan may not be required. In other words, if the FDG-PET/CT already provides unambiguous evidence of bone involvement, the additional information from a sodium fluoride PET/CT is considered unnecessary. This guidance applies to both modalities, emphasizing that a clear positive result on FDG-PET/CT can eliminate the need for further sodium fluoride PET/CT imaging in the same clinical context.
  - Source: PET/CT SCAN
  - Target: SODIUM FLUORIDE PET/CT
  - Description: Sodium fluoride PET/CT is a form of PET/CT scan.</data>
