      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) operates the online resource CDC.gov/tobacco, which serves as the agency's dedicated digital platform for tobacco cessation. As the CDC's official online tobacco cessation resource, CDC.gov/tobacco provides information and support to help individuals quit tobacco use, reflecting the CDC's broader public health mission to reduce tobacco-related disease and death. This platform is a key component of the CDC's efforts to offer accessible cessation guidance and resources to the public.</data>
