    <edge source="MRI SCAN" target="PET/MRI SCAN" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">MRI SCAN</data>
      <data key="d8">PET/MRI SCAN</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">MRI SCAN and PET/MRI SCAN are related medical imaging entities. An MRI scan is a standalone imaging modality. A PET/MRI SCAN, as described, combines MRI imaging with PET scanning. In other words, a PET/MRI scan integrates the anatomical detail of MRI with the functional information provided by PET. Both provided descriptions are consistent and redundant, stating that a PET/MRI scan combines MRI imaging with PET/PET scanning. Therefore, the PET/MRI scan is a hybrid imaging technique that merges the two technologies into a single examination, offering complementary diagnostic capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d12">MRI SCAN</data>
    </edge>
