    <edge source="CARE TEAM" target="FAMILY MEMBERS" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d8">FAMILY MEMBERS</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The care team asks about the health history of family members who are blood relatives.</data>
      <data key="d12">FAMILY MEMBERS</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARE TEAM" target="MEDICAL HISTORY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d8">MEDICAL HISTORY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The care team uses the patient's medical history to help determine which treatment is best. By reviewing the medical history, the care team can assess relevant health information and make informed decisions about the most appropriate course of treatment for the patient.</data>
      <data key="d12">MEDICAL HISTORY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARE TEAM" target="TREATMENTS" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d8">TREATMENTS</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The care team may prescribe medicines and determine which treatment is best for the patient.</data>
      <data key="d12">TREATMENTS</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARE TEAM" target="FAMILY HISTORY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d8">FAMILY HISTORY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The care team asks about the health history of blood relatives (family history)</data>
      <data key="d12">FAMILY HISTORY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARE TEAM" target="HEALTH CARE PROVIDER" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d8">HEALTH CARE PROVIDER</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The care team is a collaborative group that includes health care providers as integral members. Health care providers are part of the care team, serving as members who contribute to the team's overall function. In essence, the health care provider is a constituent of the care team, with both descriptions emphasizing that providers belong to and participate within the care team structure.</data>
      <data key="d12">HEALTH CARE PROVIDER</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARE TEAM" target="GENETIC TESTING" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d8">GENETIC TESTING</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The care team focuses on assessing cancer risk by inquiring about family history and the use of genetic testing. Specifically, they ask whether family members have undergone genetic testing, as this information helps clarify hereditary risk and guide patient care.</data>
      <data key="d12">GENETIC TESTING</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARE TEAM" target="BIOPSY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d8">BIOPSY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The care team orders and uses biopsy results as part of diagnosis and treatment</data>
      <data key="d12">BIOPSY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARE TEAM" target="CHEMOTHERAPY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d8">CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The care team helps manage side effects such as nausea and vomiting during chemotherapy.</data>
      <data key="d12">CARE TEAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARE TEAM" target="PATIENT" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d8">PATIENT</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The CARE TEAM and the PATIENT work together as partners in the patients healthcare journey. The care team is responsible for assembling and reviewing test results, using this information to manage and coordinate the patients ongoing care. In this collaborative relationship, the patient actively participates by discussing test results with the care team and following the recommendations provided. The patient is encouraged to communicate openly with the care team, share symptoms and concerns, and help the care team get to know them as an individual. In return, the care team provides care, guidance, and management based on the patients unique needs. Together, the CARE TEAM and the PATIENT form a cooperative unit focused on achieving the best possible health outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d12">CARE TEAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARE TEAM" target="DOCTOR" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d8">DOCTOR</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The doctor is a member of the patient's care team. The care team includes the doctor as part of the patient's care team. Therefore, the doctor and the care team are connected: the doctor participates in the care team, which is responsible for the patient's care.</data>
      <data key="d12">CARE TEAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARE TEAM" target="CLINICAL TRIAL" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d8">CLINICAL TRIAL</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The care team can be consulted to determine whether a patient qualifies for an available clinical trial.</data>
      <data key="d12">CARE TEAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARE TEAM" target="BLOOD TESTS" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d8">BLOOD TESTS</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The care team is responsible for ordering and interpreting blood tests as part of the overall diagnosis and treatment process. In addition, the care team orders and reviews blood tests along with imaging results and reports, ensuring that all diagnostic information is evaluated together to guide patient care.</data>
      <data key="d12">CARE TEAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARE TEAM" target="CT SCAN" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d8">CT SCAN</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Patients should tell their care team about past allergic reactions to contrast, which is often used for CT scans.</data>
      <data key="d12">CARE TEAM</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="CARE TEAM" target="MRI" id="related_to">
