    <edge source="CHEMOTHERAPY" target="FOLFOX" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d8">FOLFOX</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">FOLFOX is a chemotherapy regimen used in the treatment of certain cancers. As part of the broader category of chemotherapy, FOLFOX combines multiple anti-cancer drugs and is administered intravenously. It is specifically indicated as a treatment option for metastatic anal cancer, offering a systemic approach for patients with advanced disease. Additionally, FOLFOX is recommended as a chemotherapy regimen for high-risk stage 2 and stage 3 colon cancers, where it is used to reduce the risk of recurrence after surgical resection. Thus, FOLFOX serves as a versatile chemotherapy protocol in oncology, applied across different gastrointestinal malignancies depending on disease stage and clinical context.</data>
      <data key="d12">FOLFOX</data>
    </edge>
