    <edge source="PROGRESSION" target="CHEMOTHERAPY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">PROGRESSION</data>
      <data key="d8">CHEMOTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Cancer progression can occur during or after chemotherapy treatment.</data>
      <data key="d12">PROGRESSION</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="PROGRESSION" target="IMMUNOTHERAPY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">PROGRESSION</data>
      <data key="d8">IMMUNOTHERAPY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">For patients whose cancer shows progression either during or after chemotherapy, immunotherapy is recommended as the next line of treatment for those who are eligible. This approach applies when the disease advances despite or following completion of chemotherapy, establishing immunotherapy as the standard subsequent therapeutic option.</data>
      <data key="d12">PROGRESSION</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FAMILY HISTORY" target="MEDICAL HISTORY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">FAMILY HISTORY</data>
      <data key="d8">MEDICAL HISTORY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Medical history includes family history.</data>
      <data key="d12">FAMILY HISTORY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FAMILY HISTORY" target="CARE TEAM" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">FAMILY HISTORY</data>
      <data key="d8">CARE TEAM</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The care team is responsible for collecting and reviewing information related to family history as part of patient assessments. Specifically, the care team asks about family history, gathering details about the patient's relatives and their health conditions. This process is also described as asking about the family medical history, meaning the care team solicits information regarding any medical conditions, diseases, or health patterns that may run in the patient's family. In practice, the care team's inquiry into family history encompasses the broader family medical history, ensuring that relevant hereditary and genetic factors are considered in the patient's overall care plan.</data>
      <data key="d12">FAMILY HISTORY</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="FAMILY HISTORY" target="GENETIC TESTING" id="related_to">
