      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Cirrhosis is a major risk factor for the development of liver cancer. It is formally listed as a risk factor for liver cancer, and clinical comparisons are often made between individuals who have cirrhosis and those who do not, highlighting the elevated risk associated with the condition. In this context, cirrhosis and liver cancer are closely linked, with cirrhosis representing a significant predisposing condition for the onset of liver cancer.</data>
      <data key="d12">LIVER CANCER</data>
    </edge>
