      <data key="d8">TMB-H</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Both TMB-H and MSI-H/dMMR are tumor mutation statuses that may guide treatment with immunotherapy drugs.</data>
      <data key="d12">MSI-H/DMMR MUTATION</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MSI-H/DMMR MUTATION" target="MICROSATELLITE INSTABILITY" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">MSI-H/DMMR MUTATION</data>
      <data key="d8">MICROSATELLITE INSTABILITY</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">MSI-H/dMMR mutation is a type of DNA change that leads to microsatellite instability-high or deficient mismatch repair. Microsatellite instability is a characteristic feature of MSI-H/dMMR mutation. In other words, the MSI-H/dMMR mutation drives the development of microsatellite instability, making the two closely related in the context of genomic alterations.</data>
      <data key="d12">MSI-H/DMMR MUTATION</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="MSI-H/DMMR MUTATION" target="DEFICIENT MISMATCH REPAIR" id="related_to">
