    <edge source="NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK" target="APL" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">NATIONAL COMPREHENSIVE CANCER NETWORK</data>
      <data key="d8">APL</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">The National Comprehensive Cancer Network (NCCN) provides patient-focused guidance that covers acute promyelocytic leukemia (APL). Specifically, the NCCN Guidelines for Patients include a dedicated chapter on the treatment of APL. This chapter is part of the organization's broader patient education materials, which translate the clinical NCCN Guidelines into accessible information for individuals affected by cancer. The inclusion of APL treatment in the NCCN patient guidelines reflects the network's commitment to helping patients understand standard care options for this specific leukemia subtype. Both descriptions affirm the same fact: the NCCNs patient guide contains a treatment-focused chapter on APL.</data>
      <data key="d12">APL</data>
    </edge>
