    <edge source="RADICAL CYSTECTOMY" target="URINARY DIVERSION" id="related_to">
      <data key="d7">RADICAL CYSTECTOMY</data>
      <data key="d8">URINARY DIVERSION</data>
      <data key="d9">related_to</data>
      <data key="d10">1.0</data>
      <data key="d11">Radical cystectomy is a surgical procedure that involves the removal of the bladder. Urinary diversion is a complementary surgical procedure performed at the same time as radical cystectomy, designed to provide a new way for urine to leave the body. Together, these procedures ensure that, after the bladder is removed, a functional pathway for urine excretion is established. Urinary diversion is thus an integral part of the overall surgical management when radical cystectomy is performed.</data>
      <data key="d12">RADICAL CYSTECTOMY</data>
    </edge>
